        "name": null,
        "patch_url": null
      },
      "body": "I think this is misguided. Signing and verification are just two examples of functions that use the tables. The description should be more generic and differentiate between API functions which cannot the static context (e.g., signing, key gen, ecdh, ...) and those which can.  Though it's a still a bit hard to describe because we the latter includes functions which use the `ecmult` table and some that don't use any table (and in the API docs we rightly don't say anything about this). It's probably good enough to roughly list those here that require the ecmult table (anything else than verification?) ",
